<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vet River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vet River is a river of the Free State province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> and a tributary of the Vaal. In the 1830s Voortrekker parties settled the land between the Vet and the Vaal, where the town of Winburg became the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> centre north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-river">Orange River</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vet-river.jpg" alt="Vet River" width="320" height="107" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hermanerasmus · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bloemhof_Dam._View_from_the_Freestate_side.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
